:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Plugin Reference",
    title: "HamlPlugin",
    summary: "HamlPlugin turns `.haml` files into Ruby component classes with imports, source maps, companion styles, and optional translations."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Component Output" }
    :markdown
      A Haml module exports a component class as `Default`. The generated class inherits from the configured component base class and renders through the configured factory.

      ```ruby
      Klenod::Build::Plugins::HamlPlugin.new(
        component_base_class: "Example::Component",
        factory: "Example::H"
      )
      ```

      Imported component constants can be used directly as Haml tags. `%Button` compiles to a factory call using the imported component class as the tag.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Ruby Blocks And Filters" }
    :markdown
      Top-level `:ruby` defines imports, constants, and methods on the generated component class. Later Ruby script blocks compile into the render method, where request-local helpers from the application framework are available.

      `=` prints a value, `-` runs code silently, and printed Ruby blocks such as `= if condition` render their Haml body.

      Haml `:markdown` filters are delegated to `MarkdownPlugin`. Haml `:css` filters become inline CSS sources collected from the template.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Companions" }
    :markdown
      Haml automatically watches and imports matching CSS companions as `Styles`.

      ```text
      components/Card.haml
      components/Card.css

      pages/docs/+page.haml
      pages/docs/+page.css
      ```

      Translation companions use `IntlPlugin`. Haml can run without `IntlPlugin`; in that case the generated component receives an empty translation map.

      ```text
      components/Card.intl.en.toml
      components/Card.intl.sv.toml
      ```

  %DocsSection{ title: "Errors" }
    :markdown
      Generated Ruby includes source map marks. Runtime backtraces can be rewritten to original Haml files and parse errors show Haml source context without requiring users to inspect generated Ruby.
